c Debt. Face value. 2 Sources: Federal Reserve Bulletin, table 1.18, Federal Reserve Banks, statement of condition, for System Open Market Accounts; and U. S. Treasury for government accounts. Federal Reserve holdings exclude Treasury securities held under repurchase agreements. 3 Source: Federal Reserve Board of Governors, Flow of Funds Table L.209. 4 Includes commercial banks, savings institutions and credit unions. 5 Source: U.S. Treasury Monthly Statement of Public Debt. Current accrual value. 6 Includes U.S. Treasury securities held by the Federal Employees Retirement System Thrift Savings Plan \\u201cG Fund.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"footnote\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [831, 1702, 1506, 1893], \"page_id\": 51}], \"content\": \"7 Includes money market mutual funds, mutual funds and closed-end investment companies. 8 Source: Federal Reserve Board Treasury International Capital Survey. Includes nonmarketable foreign series Treasury securities and Treasury deposit funds. Excludes Treasury securities held under repurchase agreements in custody accounts at the Federal Reserve Bank of New York. Estimates reflect the 1984 benchmark to December 1989, the 1989 benchmark to December 1994 and the 1994 benchmark to date. 9 Includes individuals, Government-sponsored enterprises, brokers and dealers, bank personal trusts and estates, corporate and non-corporate businesses, and other investors. Note.\\u2014Ownership data have been revised back to March 1989 in order to update ownership categories and to incorporate greater reliance on Flow of Funds data of the Federal Reserve Board.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"footnote\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [142, 85, 173, 108], \"page_id\": 52}], \"content\": \"50\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [537, 196, 1087, 229], \"page_id\": 52}], \"content\": \"INTRODUCTION: Market Yields\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [137, 280, 800, 401], \"page_id\": 52}], \"content\": \"The tables and charts in this section present yields on Treasury marketable securities, and compare long-term yields on Treasury securities with yields on long-term corporate and municipal securities.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [137, 403, 796, 561], \"page_id\": 52}], \"content\": \"Table MY-1 lists Treasury market bid yields at constant maturities for bills, notes and bonds. The Treasury yield curve in the accompanying chart is based on current market bid quotations on the most actively traded Treasury securities as of 3:30 p.m. on the last business day of the calendar quarter.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [140, 556, 798, 740], \"page_id\": 52}], \"content\": \"The Treasury uses quotations obtained by the FRB of New York to derive the yield curve, based on semiannual interest payments and read at constant maturity points to develop a consistent data series. Yields on Treasury bills are coupon equivalent yields of bank discount rates at which Treasury bills trade in the market. The Board of Governors of the Fed-\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [838, 280, 1486, 342], \"page_id\": 52}], \"content\": \"eral Reserve System publishes the Treasury constant maturity data series in its weekly H.15 press release.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [836, 344, 1488, 712], \"page_id\": 52}], \"content\": \"Table MY-2 shows average yields of long-term Treasury, corporate and municipal bonds. The long-term Treasury average yield is the 30-year constant maturity yield. The corporate bond average yield is developed by Treasury by calculating reoffering yields on new long-term securities maturing in at least 20 years and rated Aa by Moody's Investors Service. The municipal bond average yield prior to 1991 was compiled by Treasury. Beginning with January 1991, the average yield is the \\\"Municipal Bond Yield Average,\\\" published by Moody's Investors Service for 20-year reoffering yields on selected Aa-rated general obligations. See the footnotes for further explanation.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [177, 766, 1461, 804], \"page_id\": 52}], \"content\": \"TABLE MY-1.\\u2014Treasury Market Bid Yields at Constant Maturities: Bills, Notes and Bonds*\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 7, \"type\": \"caption\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [446, 823, 1191, 858], \"page_id\": 52}], \"content\": \"[In percentages. Source: Office of Market Finance, Office of the Under Secretary for Domestic Finance]\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 8, \"type\": \"caption\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [140, 865, 1495, 1775], \"page_id\": 52}], \"content\": \"<table><tr><th>Date</th><th>3-mo. (1)</th><th>6-mo. (2)</th><th>1-yr. (3)</th><th>2-yr. (4)</th><th>3-yr. (5)</th><th>5-yr. (6)</th><th>7-yr. (7)</th><th>10-yr. (8)</th><th>30-yr. (9)</th></tr><tr><td colspan=\\\"10\\\">Monthly average:</td></tr><tr><td>1998 - Apr.</td><td>5.08</td><td>5.26</td><td>5.38</td><td>5.56</td><td>5.58</td><td>5.61</td><td>5.70</td><td>5.64</td><td>5.92</td></tr><tr><td>May</td><td>5.14</td><td>5.36</td><td>5.44</td><td>5.59</td><td>5.61</td><td>5.63</td><td>5.72</td><td>5.65</td><td>5.93</td></tr><tr><td>June</td><td>5.12</td><td>5.32</td><td>5.41</td><td>5.52</td><td>5.52</td><td>5.52</td><td>5.56</td><td>5.50</td><td>5.70</td></tr><tr><td>July</td><td>5.09</td><td>5.23</td><td>5.36</td><td>5.46</td><td>5.47</td><td>5.46</td><td>5.52</td><td>5.46</td><td>5.68</td></tr><tr><td>Aug.</td><td>5.04</td><td>5.15</td><td>5.21</td><td>5.27</td><td>5.24</td><td>5.27</td><td>5.36</td><td>5.34</td><td>5.54</td></tr><tr><td>Sept.</td><td>4.74</td><td>4.81</td><td>4.71</td><td>4.67</td><td>4.62</td><td>4.62</td><td>4.76</td><td>4.81</td><td>5.20</td></tr><tr><td>