\": \"7 Includes money market mutual funds, mutual funds, and closed-end investment companies.\\n8 Source: Federal Reserve Board Treasury International Capital Survey. Includes nonmarketable foreign series, Treasury securities, and Treasury deposit funds. Excludes Treasury securities held under repurchase agreements in custody accounts at the Federal Reserve Bank of New York. For additional information see: http://www.treas.gov/tic/ticsec2.shtml.\\n9 Includes individuals, Government-sponsored enterprises, brokers and dealers, bank personal trusts and estates, corporate and non-corporate businesses, and other investors.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"footnote\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [1379, 1987, 1501, 2022], \"page_id\": 48}], \"content\": \"June 2009\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 7, \"type\": \"page_footer\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [140, 94, 173, 127], \"page_id\": 49}], \"content\": \"42\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [541, 212, 1091, 250], \"page_id\": 49}], \"content\": \"INTRODUCTION: Market Yields\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [138, 266, 800, 361], \"page_id\": 49}], \"content\": \"The table in this section presents yields on Treasury marketable securities for maturities ranging from 1 month to 30 years.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [142, 368, 800, 676], \"page_id\": 49}], \"content\": \"Table MY-1 lists Treasury market bid yields at constant maturities for bills, notes, and bonds. These Constant Maturity Treasury rates (CMTs) are interpolated from the Treasury yield curve and published daily at Treasury's Domestic Finance web site, www.ustreas.gov/offices/domestic-finance/debt-management/interest-rate/yield.shtml. The yield curve is fitted daily using a hermite cubic spline. For inputs, Treasury primarily uses the bid yields of the on-the-run securities (most recently auctioned Treasury securities in all maturity tranches that Treasury currently auctions) as\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [829, 266, 1492, 391], \"page_id\": 49}], \"content\": \"quoted in the secondary bond market as of approximately 3:30 p.m. each trading day. CMT yields are based on semiannual interest payments and are read at constant maturity points to develop a consistent data series.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [829, 396, 1492, 552], \"page_id\": 49}], \"content\": \"The quotations used by Treasury to calculate the bid yields and fit the yield curve are obtained by the Federal Reserve Bank of New York. The Board of Governors of the Federal Reserve System also publishes the Treasury constant maturity data series in its weekly Statistical Release H.15.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [829, 559, 1492, 679], \"page_id\": 49}], \"content\": \"Treasury discontinued the 30-year constant maturity yield during the time period February 18, 2002, through February 8, 2006. Thus, 30-year yields for that time frame are not available.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [330, 771, 1290, 844], \"page_id\": 49}], \"content\": \"TABLE MY-1.\\u2014Treasury Market Bid Yields at Constant Maturities: Bills, Notes, and Bonds*\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 7, \"type\": \"caption\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [426, 853, 1186, 879], \"page_id\": 49}], \"content\": \"[In percentages. Source: Office of Debt Management, Office of the Under Secretary for Domestic Finance]\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 8, \"type\": \"caption\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [142, 879, 1472, 1754], \"page_id\": 49}], \"content\": \"<table><tr><th>Period</th><th>1-mo. (1)</th><th>3-mo. (2)</th><th>6-mo. (3)</th><th>1-yr. (4)</th><th>2-yr. (5)</th><th>3-yr. (6)</th><th>5-yr. (7)</th><th>7-yr. (8)</th><th