{"type":"message","message":{"id":"gen-1775253872-1nTMwLruaGOQoIxgdkhn","role":"assistant","created":1775253920,"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Python 3.12 is available but numpy is not installed. Let me try a manual approach for polynomial regression.\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_4b8171293f865a56","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"shell","arguments":{"command":"python3 << 'EOF'\n# Manual cubic polynomial regression without numpy\n\n# Historical surplus/deficit data (1989-2013)\nyears = [1989, 1990, 1991, 1992, 1993, 1994, 1995, 1996, 1997, 1998, \n         1999, 2000, 2001, 2002, 2003, 2004, 2005, 2006, 2007, 2008, \n         2009, 2010, 2011, 2012, 2013]\n\n# Surplus/deficit values from the bulletins (in millions)\ny = [\n    -152087,   # 1989\n    -220388,   # 1990\n    -268729,   # 1991\n    -290204,   # 1992\n    -254948,   # 1993\n    -203370,   # 1994\n    -163813,   # 1995\n    -107331,   # 1996\n    -22618,    # 1997\n    70039,     # 1998\n    125974,    # 1999\n    236917,    # 2000\n    127401,    # 2001\n    -157823,   # 2002\n    -374791,   # 2003\n    -412986,   # 2004\n    -318298,   # 2005\n    -248197,   # 2006\n    -161527,   # 2007\n    -454798,   # 2008\n    -1415722,  # 2009\n    -1294204,  # 2010\n    -1295591,  # 2011\n    -1089353,  # 2012\n    -680276    # 2013\n]\n\n# Center the years to avoid overflow issues\nyear_offset = 2000\nx = [yi - year_offset for yi in years]\n\n# Build the normal equations for cubic polynomial\n# y = a*x^3 + b*x^2 + c*x + d\nn = len(x)\n\n# Calculate sums\nsx = sum(x)\nsx2 = sum([xi**2 for xi in x])\nsx3 = sum([xi**3 for xi in x])\nsx4 = sum([xi**4 for xi in x])\nsx5 = sum([xi**5 for xi in x])\nsx6 = sum([xi**6 for xi in x])\n\nsy = sum(y)\nsxy = sum([x[i]*y[i] for i in range(n)])\nsx2y = sum([x[i]**2*y[i] for i in range(n)])\nsx3y = sum([x[i]**3*y[i] for i in range(n)])\n\n# Build the matrix for normal equations\n# [n, sx, sx2, sx3] [d]   [sy]\n# [sx, sx2, sx3, sx4] [b] = [sxy]\n# [sx2, sx3, sx4, sx5] [a]   [sx2y]\n# [sx3, sx4, sx5, sx6] [c]   [sx3y]\n\nimport math\n\n# Use Cramer's rule to solve the 4x4 system\ndef det4(m):\n    return (m[0][0]*((m[1][1]*m[2][2]*m[3][3] + m[1][2]*m[2][3]*m[3][1] + m[1][3]*m[2][1]*m[3][2]) \n                     - (m[1][1]*m[2][3]*m[3][2] + m[1][2]*m[2][1]*m[3][3] + m[1][3]*m[2][2]*m[3][1]))\n          - m[0][1]*((m[1][0]*m[2][2]*m[3][3] + m[1][2]*m[2][3]*m[3][0] + m[1][3]*m[2][0]*m[3][2])\n                     - (m[1][0]*m[2][3]*m[3][2] + m[1][2]*m[2][0]*m[3][3] + m[1][3]*m[2][2]*m[3][0]))\n          + m[0][2]*((m[1][0]*m[2][1]*m[3][3] + m[1][1]*m[2][3]*m[3][0] + m[1][3]*m[2][0]*m[3][1])\n                     - (m[1][0]*m[2][3]*m[3][1] + m[1][1]*m[2][0]*m[3][3] + m[1][3]*m[2][1]*m[3][0]))\n          - m[0][3]*((m[1][0]*m[2][1]*m[3][2] + m[1][1]*m[2][2]*m[3][0] + m[1][2]*m[2][0]*m[3][1])\n                     - (m[1][0]*m[2][2]*m[3][1] + m[1][1]*m[2][0]*m[3][2] + m[1][2]*m[2][1]*m[3][0])))\n\n# Matrix A for the coefficient matrix\nA = [\n    [n, sx, sx2, sx3],\n    [sx, sx2, sx3, sx4],\n    [sx2, sx3, sx4, sx5],\n    [sx3, sx4, sx5, sx6]\n]\n\n# Right hand side vector\nB = [sy, sxy, sx2y, sx3y]\n\n# Determinant of A\ndetA = det4(A)\n\n# Replace column k with B to find determinant for each coefficient\nA0 = [[B[i] if j == 0 else A[i][j] for j in range(4)] for i in range(4)]\ndetA0 = det4(A0)\n\nA1 = [[B[i] if j == 1 else A[i][j] for j in range(4)] for i in range(4)]\ndetA1 = det4(A1)\n\nA2 = [[B[i] if j == 2 else A[i][j] for j in range(4)] for i in range(4)]\ndetA2 = det4(A2)\n\nA3 = [[B[i] if j == 3 else A[i][j] for j in range(4)] for i in range(4)]\ndetA3 = det4(A3)\n\n# Solve for coefficients\nd = detA0 / detA\nb = detA1 / detA\na = detA2 / detA\nc = detA3 / detA\n\nprint(f\"Cubic polynomial: y = {a:.6f}*x^3 + {b:.6f}*x^2 + {c:.6f}*x + {d:.6f}\")\nprint(f\"where x = year - {year_offset}\")\n\n# Predict for year 2025\nx_2025 = 2025 - year_offset\ny_2025 = a*x_2025**3 + b*x_2025**2 + c*x_2025 + d\n\nprint(f\"\\nPredicted surplus/deficit for 2025: {y_2025:.2f} million dollars\")\n\n# Check fit by computing R-squared\ny_pred = [a*xi**3 + b*xi**2 + c*xi + d for xi in x]\ny_mean = sum(y)/len(y)\nss_res = sum([(y[i] - y_pred[i])**2 for i in range(n)])\nss_tot = sum([(yi - y_mean)**2 for yi in y])\nr_squared = 1 - ss_res/ss_tot\n\nprint(f\"R-squared: {r_squared:.6f}\")\nEOF"}}},"_meta":{"goose_extension":"developer"}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
